              note: "Federal unemployment tax (FUTA, IRC section 3301): 6.0% of the first $7,000 of each employee's wages a year from each employer, less a credit of up to 5.4% for state unemployment tax paid (so 0.6% net), the credit cut by a credit-reduction state's reduction (regions.json). A liability over $500 is deposited by the last day of the month after its quarter, less carries to the next; the annual return (Form 940) settles the rest by 31 January."
